#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:5
#: 6db62695d8244e02bede1e9bce07d9cb
msgid "Limit Cycle Detection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:7
#: 515fbbf7fddf4614a870ec0d1e2535dd
msgid "ArduPilot provides a limit cycle detection feature to help reduce or eliminate oscillations in the control loops due to excessive tuning gains. The algorithm monitors the actuator slew rates, and if above limits set by the _SMAX parameters, will lower the control loop gains in an attempt to stop the oscillations. These parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:9
#: 5862b777827e41c58b86f6f54761ecb4
msgid ":ref:`PTCH_RATE_SMAX<PTCH_RATE_SMAX>` for pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:10
#: 9456cbc90b30402eb5f6e49034e4ca1c
msgid ":ref:`RLL_RATE_SMAX<RLL_RATE_SMAX>` for roll"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:12
#: 75ae7436cc204828be556078d31a9fd6
msgid "for the Pitch and Roll control surface detection limits on fixed wing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:16
#: 7dc91aae2bf24b2ba5a04fa852892556
msgid "The limit should be set to no more than 25% of the actuator's maximum slew rate to allow for load effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:19
#: a454055199fe41f7a3f6177cd998d3ab
msgid "For example, for most servos which specify a 0.1s speed for 60 deg deflection (600deg/s), the value should be no more than 150, which is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:21
#: 7e6ff06f343142a7b92f6623a3b54692
msgid "For QuadPlane actuators (motors,surfaces,tilt servos depending on frame type):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:23
#: bb4eb2208a2f427e9cb40cebdb7fd2a2
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_SMAX<Q_A_RAT_PIT_SMAX>` for VTOL pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:24
#: 2c36c7003ea449c9b2ee53d0ceadaede
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_SMAX<Q_A_RAT_RLL_SMAX>` for VTOL roll"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:25
#: c47d19b6e88045cfbfaf0f780c003e82
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_YAW_SMAX<Q_A_RAT_YAW_SMAX>` for VTOL yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:26
#: 2a7e9ebed0444e649010ba146ece3f69
msgid ":ref:`Q_P_D_ACC_SMAX<Q_P_D_ACC_SMAX>` for VTOL position control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:28
#: 9a85d7fc0deb447f87d304e3ba6904f2
msgid "These are in different units (full activations per second), and have 50 as the default, which effectively de-activates them because they are too high. Currently, setting these such that they are active interferes with the QAUTOTUNE and this will be corrected in the future, but it allows logging of the actual slew rates in the PIQx.SRate log messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo-limit-cycle-detection.rst:30
#: d6709a889eb344f9b0e241f461728d24
msgid "When these values are exceeded, the appropriate PID Dmod log data ( PIDR.Dmod, PIQP.DMod, etc.)will show values spiking below 1 in the plots, indicating lowered gains. An ideal tune, will have this occur very occasionally during operation, but not frequently. By examining the logged PIDx.SRate messages one can see the actual slew rates being used and set these _ SMAX values appropriately to be at or slightly above the general peak slew rates."
msgstr ""

